
For us to continue with the application please send us an original full birth or adoption certificate for issued by the relevant authority, or a replacement obtained from them. This must show their parent or adoptive parent details.

If the documents are not in English you must also send us an English translation. This must be attached to the original document and signed by the translator to confirm that it is a true copy of the original.

The translator must be:

registered with an official organisation like the Institute of Linguistics or the Institute of Translation and Interpreting
employed by a recognised translation company (for example, a member of the Association of Translation companies)
if overseas, employed by a translation company listed on the British Embassy/High Commission or British Consulate website
The translator cannot be a family member or friend.



